[[:db/retract 17592186117505 :answer-field/choices 17592186117506] [:db/retract 17592186117505 :answer-field/choices 17592186117507] [:db/retract 17592186117505 :answer-field/choices 17592186117508] [:db/retract 17592186117505 :answer-field/choices 17592186117509] [:db/retract 17592186117505 :answer-field/choices 17592186117510] {:db/id 17592186120224 :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,-3,5)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(3,2,-8)$ and $B(1,2,-5).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,-3,5⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(3,2,-8)$ and $B(1,2,-5)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,2,-5⟩-⟨3,2,-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-2,0,3⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,3⟩ & =⟨2,-3,5⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,0,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,3⟩ & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186117505 :answer-field/correct "answer-8f5b6228-4151-5fb7-a8b8-4defb3112da4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f5b6228-4151-5fb7-a8b8-4defb3112da4" "answer-b05ca4a9-4343-56a3-86ae-980793c8602f" "answer-7a8f836e-b1bd-5929-a0d4-cc62e2406547" "answer-f59eba3d-6e2f-504f-905a-a227d63c2c42" "answer-ab54b251-064b-57d4-8fc1-3a45c6f498e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f5b6228-4151-5fb7-a8b8-4defb3112da4" :answer/id #uuid "8f5b6228-4151-5fb7-a8b8-4defb3112da4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,3⟩=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b05ca4a9-4343-56a3-86ae-980793c8602f" :answer/id #uuid "b05ca4a9-4343-56a3-86ae-980793c8602f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,0,3⟩=⟨2,-3,5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a8f836e-b1bd-5929-a0d4-cc62e2406547" :answer/id #uuid "7a8f836e-b1bd-5929-a0d4-cc62e2406547" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f59eba3d-6e2f-504f-905a-a227d63c2c42" :answer/id #uuid "f59eba3d-6e2f-504f-905a-a227d63c2c42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab54b251-064b-57d4-8fc1-3a45c6f498e7" :answer/id #uuid "ab54b251-064b-57d4-8fc1-3a45c6f498e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=⟨-2,0,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3fa29ff6-5ae4-5642-82fd-03b1645e810c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3fa29ff6-5ae4-5642-82fd-03b1645e810c" :question/id #uuid "3fa29ff6-5ae4-5642-82fd-03b1645e810c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127921" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨5,-1,3⟩=27.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨5,-1,3⟩=27$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨5,-1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =5{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,5{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f9a0d8dd-871f-5fc8-9699-7a78c5f80aac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f9a0d8dd-871f-5fc8-9699-7a78c5f80aac" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a0d8dd-871f-5fc8-9699-7a78c5f80aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-36cb63bc-ae79-51e4-b5ab-3039c42340e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36cb63bc-ae79-51e4-b5ab-3039c42340e0" "answer-502b671f-b1be-5d29-8f96-08571a87d173" "answer-1b182a09-cc9d-51c4-95fe-e78790ecf72a" "answer-72001519-6957-56f0-b511-f27a9ed3c85f" "answer-4173b538-e381-5dd5-b0c5-10dc2eaa96c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36cb63bc-ae79-51e4-b5ab-3039c42340e0" :answer/id #uuid "36cb63bc-ae79-51e4-b5ab-3039c42340e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-502b671f-b1be-5d29-8f96-08571a87d173" :answer/id #uuid "502b671f-b1be-5d29-8f96-08571a87d173" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b182a09-cc9d-51c4-95fe-e78790ecf72a" :answer/id #uuid "1b182a09-cc9d-51c4-95fe-e78790ecf72a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72001519-6957-56f0-b511-f27a9ed3c85f" :answer/id #uuid "72001519-6957-56f0-b511-f27a9ed3c85f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4173b538-e381-5dd5-b0c5-10dc2eaa96c4" :answer/id #uuid "4173b538-e381-5dd5-b0c5-10dc2eaa96c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-77095dee-04b2-5198-bba9-43f589fc9964" :activity/id #uuid "77095dee-04b2-5198-bba9-43f589fc9964" :activity/title "The Vector Equation of a Plane" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049436 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-8d1b2442-6684-5f23-a6d5-881beb105644" "step-6262b847-bfad-5541-b7d9-0c48d99eb024" "step-6f1edd60-137